    "narrative": "The anchor of today's lineup is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who at a 75.30 efficiency score, represents our most reliable engine against Suarez. His placement in the #2 hole provides optimal leverage to capitalize on base runners, while **Lawrence Butler** follows closely at 73.47. **Lawrence Butler** is a priority start today due to a rare convergence of a favorable park shift and a +13% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage against Lambert, making him an elite play despite the pitcher's moderate xERA. Additionally, **Kyle Karros** earns a surprisingly strong 63.20 rating; beyond his park and platoon edge, his ability to capitalize on the opposing pitcher's slow delivery provides a nuanced SB potential that fits our team's strategic emphasis on speed.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Masyn Winn**, who landed at 36.35, falling well below our 40-point efficiency floor. While his speed profile is highly desirable, the matchup against Skenes is a brutal gauntlet that suppresses his ceiling. The negative modifiers regarding the elite catcher pop time and Skenes\u2019 propensity for holding runners made **Masyn Winn** an easy fade compared to the higher-floor options like **Cal Raleigh** or **Yainer Diaz**. We are also keeping a close watch on **JJ Bleday**, whose 42.98 score is dangerously close to the benching threshold; the -14% penalty from his platoon disadvantage is a significant drag, and he remains the most likely candidate for a mid-game defensive substitution if the score tightens.",
